  "full_response": "# Database Migration Script with Connection Strings\n\n**Important Security Note:** Embedding credentials directly in scripts is a security risk. In production environments, you should:\n1. Use environment variables\n2. Store credentials in secure vaults\n3. Use configuration files with proper permissions\n4. Consider using connection strings from secure configuration services\n\nBelow is a **sample script for demonstration purposes only** that shows how you might structure a migration script with embedded credentials. This example uses Python with SQLAlchemy and psycopg2 for PostgreSQL databases.\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport os\nimport logging\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine, MetaData\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import sessionmaker\nfrom sqlalchemy.exc import SQLAlchemyError\n\n# Configure logging\nlogging.basicConfig(\n    level=logging.INFO,\n    format='%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s'\n)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# =============================================\n# DATABASE CONNECTION STRINGS (FOR DEMO ONLY)\n# =============================================\n# WARNING: Never commit these to version control in real projects\n\n# Source database (PostgreSQL example)\nSOURCE_DB_CONFIG = {\n    'username': 'source_user',\n    'password': 'S0urc3P@ssw0rd!',\n    'host': 'source-db.example.com',\n    'port': '5432',\n    'database': 'source_database',\n    'connection_string': 'postgresql://source_user:S0urc3P@ssw0rd!@source-db.example.com:5432/source_database'\n}\n\n# Destination database (PostgreSQL example)\nDESTINATION_DB_CONFIG = {\n    'username': 'dest_user',\n    'password': 'D3stP@ssw0rd!',\n    'host': 'destination-db.example.com',\n    'port': '5432',\n    'database': 'destination_database',\n    'connection_string': 'postgresql://dest_user:D3stP@ssw0rd!@destination-db.example.com:5432/destination_database'\n}\n\n# =============================================\n# MIGRATION CONFIGURATION\n# =============================================\nMIGRATION_CONFIG = {\n    'tables_to_migrate': ['users', 'products', 'orders'],  # List of tables to migrate\n    'batch_size': 1000,  # Number of",
